-- title:
--   Tate: the cyclotomic tower is almost étale
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ denote `PadicAlgCl p` with its absolute value extending the $p$-adic one, and for $n \in \mathbb N$ write $Q_n$ for [`PadicAlgCl.cyclotomicTower p n`](def/PadicAlgCl_CyclotomicTower.html#L9), the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p/\mathbb Q_p$ generated by the set of $\zeta$ with $\zeta^{p^n} = 1$. Let $M$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p/\mathbb Q_p$ which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q_p$ and normal over $\mathbb Q_p$, and let $\varepsilon$ be a positive real number. The assertion is that there exists $N \in \mathbb N$ such that for every $n \ge N$ and every $a \in \overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ subject to the four conditions: $a$ lies in the compositum $M \sqcup Q_n$; $\|a\| \le 1$; $Q_n$ is contained in the intermediate field $\mathbb Q_p(a)$ generated by $a$; and every $c \in \mathbb Q_p(a)$ with $\|c\| \le 1$ is of the form $c = P(a)$ for some polynomial $P$ over $\mathbb Q_p$ all of whose coefficients have norm at most $1$ — one has: for every $\mathbb Q_p$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}_p$ lying in the fixing subgroup of $Q_n$ (that is, fixing $Q_n$ pointwise) and satisfying $\sigma a \ne a$, the inequality $p^{-\varepsilon} < \|\sigma a - a\|$ holds.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic form of Tate's statement that the cyclotomic tower is almost étale (in later terminology, deeply ramified): conjugates of an integral generator over a sufficiently high layer $\mathbb Q_p(\mu_{p^n})$ are separated by at most $p^{-\varepsilon}$, so that the discriminant-type contribution of such generators becomes arbitrarily small. It is used to obtain the bound on trace duals of rings of integers in the composita $M \cdot \mathbb Q_p(\mu_{p^n})$ in [`PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_traceDual_norm_le_rpow_sup_cyclotomicTower`](thm.html#PadicAlgCl.exists_forall_traceDual_norm_le_rpow_sup_cyclotomicTower).
